 Vroom Multiplayer Enhanced 2.0b (27.11.2026)
 Original install: Mr.Larmer, CFou. Version 2.0b: Vesuri.

 This install applies to "Vroom Multiplayer" © 1993 Lankhor.

 This install requires WHDLoad 17 or newer and RawDIC to be in the path. Both
 can be found in the WHDLoad package.
 To install from a different drive than DF0: select installation mode Expert.

 The installed program requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 0.5 MB OtherMem.
 It can be quit by pressing F10 (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").

 Options:
 CUSTOM1=1: Enhanced framerate, set in the installed icon together with CACHE.
 0 or unset keeps the original timing. On a 68020 or later the races run at a
 steady 16.7 game updates a second, whatever the CPU's speed. With 80 KB of
 free fast memory the picture is also drawn between the updates, up to one
 frame per video frame, for smoother motion. A 68000 or 68010 ignores it.
   
 If you have problems with this installation please try and get a newer
 version of this package from the WHDLoad WWW-Page. If that doesn't help try
 some Tooltypes like NOCACHE, NOAUTOVEC, EXPCHIP, NOMMU, PAL or NTSC. If
 that also fails, please inform the author via the Bug-Report-Form which
 can be accessed on the WHDLoad WWW-Page.

 For the full WHDLoad package, other installs and updates refer to:
        http://www.whdload.de/
 or     aminet:dev/misc/whdload#?
 and    aminet:game/patch/

 version 2.0b (27.11.2026) done by Vesuri
 - Enhanced framerate (Custom1=1) on 68020 and later, set in the installed icon:
   races run at a steady game speed on every CPU and, with fast memory, much
   more smoothly
 - fixed the crash in races with CPU caches on (68040, 68060)
 - added the blitter waits fast CPUs need
 - fixed too fast menu wipes and delays on fast CPUs
 - fixed the keyboard, which could miss keys

 version 1.6 (03.06.06) done by CFou!:
 - ExitKey fixed on 68000
 - 68000 problem fixed (bad whdload's flag was set)
 - New install script
 - source code included 

 version 1.5 (03.11.05) done by CFou!:
 - Another version supported (NTSC)
 - Another Track disk protection removed (thanks Xavier for bug report)
 - Decrunch routines optimized for more speed
 - Another decrunch routines relocated in fast memory
 - New install script
 - Source code included

 version 1.4 (06.03.04) done by CFou!:
 - Rawdic imager used now
 - Self-modifing code removed (Gfx bug on 68040)
 - Decrunch routine relocated in fast memory
 - New install script used
 - CFou!'s Glowicon added

 version 1.0-1.3 done by Mr.Larmer

